    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "Pan American\nPAA\nAir Mail Test\n- PAN AMERICAN FLIGHT EQUIAMENT-\nALL COVERS IN THIS EXHIBIT WERE CARRIED ON DC-3 OR DC-4 AIRERRET:\nPan American's Douglas DC-3 NC33609 (c/n 4100). (Pan American World Airways\nDC-3, INTRODULED BY PAN AMERICAN IN SEPT. 1937. USED AS LATE AS 1950.\nPAA\nOTHER AiRCRAFT USED BY PAN\nAMERICAN OR SUBSIDIARIES!\n• Avro-Anson\nb Boeing B-248\ny Boeing—B-307\nTBoeing-B-247\n฿ Catalina\n\u0026 Commodore Flying Boat\n•Curtis C-46\n• Douglas-\n-DC2½\n8 Douglas—DC-3\n\u0026 Douglas\n-DC-4\n#Lockheed Consteliation\nLockheed Electra\n•Lockheed Lodestar\n@Sikorsky\nMAIL FROM OTHER PARTS OF THE COUNTRY\nWAS CARRIED TO MIAMI BY CONNECTING\nAIRLINES. IN THIS CASE, BY EASTERN\nAIRLINES ON FLIGHT 603\nAhove: his view well\nlustrates\nconsiderable size of the DC-4. and also\nprovides a good close-up impression o\nnew\npostwar livery\nKellecting the airlines now greatly in\ncreased scope or operations, tre revised\nmotit depicts une compiet\nRight: Cabin interior of the DC-4, in\n'Sleeperette\" configuration\nwith gener\nous seat spacing and special leg rests\nDC-4, INTRODUCED JANUARY 1946\nEASTERN AIR LINES \"SILVERLINER\"\nWINGS CIGARETTE CARD, SERIES C-30"
